config BT_PRF_STORE
    bool "PRF store"
    depends on NIMBLE
    depends on FLASH
    help
      The bonding and root keys the recovery firmware and the normal
      firmware share, in a flash partition of its own
      (pbl/bluetooth/prf_store.h). It only needs the types of NimBLE.

choice BT_PRF_STORE_LAYOUT
    prompt "PRF store layout"
    depends on BT_PRF_STORE
    default BT_PRF_STORE_LAYOUT_RECORDS
    help
      How the partition is laid out. Both firmwares of a device have to
      agree on it, and it cannot change once a device is in the field:
      the recovery firmware there is not updated.

config BT_PRF_STORE_LAYOUT_RECORDS
    bool "Records"
    help
      A log of records of 140 bytes with one CRC, each holding all the
      store keeps: the last valid one is the store. For devices that
      have not shipped with the legacy layout.

config BT_PRF_STORE_LAYOUT_LEGACY
    bool "Legacy"
    help
      Entries of 256 bytes made of fields with a CRC each, one of them
      valid at a time. The layout of the devices that shipped with it:
      it carries fields nothing uses any more.

endchoice

if BT_PRF_STORE

module = BT_PRF_STORE
module-str = PRF store
source "subsys/logging/Kconfig.template.log_level"

endif
